  "source_context": "In vivo exposed/de-sheathed saphenous nerves of anaesthetised adult mice, mitochondria labelled with TMRM. VideoS1:50Hz proximal electrical stimulation with distal compound action-potential recording. VideoS2:naive animal without deliberate electrical stimulation. Independent examples, not a matched before/after pair.",
  "appearance": "VideoS1 is a grayscale fluorescence export with the original arrow and clock; VideoS2 is a red-channel fluorescence export with original10\u00b5m bar and clock. These are modality/false-colour signals, not natural tissue colour.",
  "orientation": "Foot/distal direction is right according to the source captions; proximal direction is left. No soma, terminal or entire nerve length is visible. No new metric bar is assigned to VideoS1.",
  "time": "Source clocks visibly read0,80,158seconds atS1frames0,40,79 and0,50,98seconds atS2frames0,25,49. The article Methods reports1.97s per acquired frame; the export clocks round to2s increments. Controls expose encoded-file time, not exact acquisition time. At1x encoded playback, the rounded source clocks advance approximately16x(S1) or20x(S2).",
  "modifications": "Full uncut source frames re-encoded into VP9 lossless RGB, with exact equality of every decoded RGB frame verified. No crop, scale, contrast change, retiming, synthetic interpolation, annotation, denoising or discarded frames. Three native PNG samples and a first-frame poster extracted from each original AVI.",
  "teaching_scope": "Compare stationary and moving organelles and distinguish cargo movement from an electrical impulse. The movies do not resolve microtubule motors, prove every bright profile identity without source labelling, measure human physiology, show a voltage waveform or establish population statistics from these two examples.",
